        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sam1",
          "text": "What is a Personal Injury Claim?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bam4",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sam3",
          "text": "When the negligent actions or inactions of one party causes another person harm, that person may have a personal injury claim. A personal injury claim is a civil legal matter, not a criminal prosecution by the government. The harmed person is compensated monetarily for the harm done to them.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bam6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sam5",
          "text": "Compensation for a personal injury claim is to pay for medical bills and financial expenses that are accident-related. Both current and future costs are available to a claimant. Common types of personal injury claims include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
